// A "_" followed by "{" is the head of a class pattern, not the wildcard, so
// a class named "_" is the structural sub-pattern of an @-binding: the arm
// tests the class and binds both the whole subject and the named field
// (spec/02-syntax.md, armPat and subPat; issue #762).
class _ {
    init(a, b) {
        this.a = a;
        this.b = b;
    }
}

print match _(1, 2) { case p @ _{b} => str(p.a) + "/" + str(b) case _ => "wild" };
print match 99 { case p @ _{b} => str(b) case _ => "wild" };

// STATUS: ok
// CHECK: 1/2
// CHECK: wild
